From 9e87n00000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EdgePi E87N port <local>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] spi: mt65xx: use MT7987 IPM default tick delay

The MT7987 IPM SPI controller needs a non-zero get-tick delay for reliable
interrupt completion. The vendor/OpenWrt MT7987 port initializes this value
to 2; the older generic Linux implementation leaves it at zero. Keep the
change limited to the existing private chip configuration used by this
kernel tree.

---
 drivers/spi/spi-mt65xx.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-mt65xx.c b/drivers/spi/spi-mt65xx.c
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-mt65xx.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-mt65xx.c
@@ -238,5 +238,5 @@
  */
 static const struct mtk_chip_config mtk_default_chip_info = {
 	.sample_sel = 0,
-	.tick_delay = 0,
+	.tick_delay = 2,
 };
